# The list follows from the program alone. To make a pattern out of a text the engine goes through every character, at some 330 instructions: two operations: a new text takes them out of the pot of its file, which says what one file may cost the build.
# Seven texts of 524,289 characters fit the pot of a small file; of the eighth no pattern is made and it is left to the run; a short one behind them is still found.
# const long = doubled("a", 19); new RegExp(long + "1"); .. new RegExp(long + "9"); new RegExp("z".toUpperCase());   (doubled(text, k): text = text + text, k times)
# DIAGNOSTIC: RegExpPatternNotConstant
# RUN: regexp-texts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: text /Z/
# CHECK: aaaa1/
# CHECK: aaaa7/
# CHECK-NOT: aaaa8/
# CHECK-NOT: aaaa9/

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
